            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Merge Sort",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Split in half, sort each, ==merge== two sorted halves with two pointers",
                "Always ==O(n log n)==, extra space O(n), {green:stable}",
                "Ties: take from the ==left half== first (`<=`)",
                "`<` on ties {red:breaks stability}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "if left[i] <= right[j]:",
                "    out.append(left[i]); i += 1",
                "else:",
                "    out.append(right[j]); j += 1"
              ],
              "note": "<= keeps equal keys in order"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Quick Sort",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pick a ==pivot==, partition into smaller and larger, recurse",
                "Average ==O(n log n)==, worst {red:O(n²)}",
                "In place, O(log n) stack, {red:not stable}",
                "Worst case: ==sorted input== with first/last pivot",
                "Fix: ==random== or ==median-of-three== pivot"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Bound the stack",
              "text": "Recurse on the ==smaller side==, loop on the larger: O(log n) stack worst case."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which to Pick",
              "ink": "purple"
